==Estonian==

===Etymology===
From {{proto|Finno-Ugric|śata|hundred|lang=et}}. Cognates include Hungarian {{term|száz|lang=hu}} and Finish {{term|sata|lang=fi}}. Originally borrowed from an {{etyl|iir|et}} language; compare Avestan {{term|sc=Avst|𐬯𐬀𐬙𐬀|tr=sata|lang=ae}}, Sanskrit {{term|sc=Deva|शत|tr=śatá|lang=sa}}.

